      "writtenOn": "2021-12-14T06:06:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TL;DR: OK, but I\u0027m resistant to it here. I\u0027ve done it anyway for your review.\n\n\nIn general I agree with this sentiment only for public-visibility APIs, whereas this is a private function that should only be called via one of the two public functions of same name.\n\nI also think given the size of this package, we\u0027re polluting the namespace with a new enum. (Also, reusing the existing HostSupported and DeviceSupported enum does not make sense here).\n\nFurthermore, I don\u0027t think golang\u0027s support of enums is sufficient for this type of API guarding; I can add pass any int as an argument; golang doesn\u0027t complain. \n\nI\u0027m not going to implement DEVICE at this time, because I have not bothered with a test case nor manual verification for it.",
